From: Matthew Zhao <matthewzhaocc@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 02:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] recovery: a node joining another node's grace expects no
 reclaims

In a rados_cluster cluster, a node that didn't restart enters grace from
its reaper when another node starts a cluster-wide one
(rados_cluster_maybe_start_grace -> nfs_start_grace(EVENT_JUST_GRACE)).
nfs_start_grace() loads no client list for EVENT_JUST_GRACE, and nothing
clears the one from the node's own last grace period (only a grace
period this node starts does), so nfs_try_lift_grace() compares the
RECLAIM_COMPLETE count and the client count left from then. Its clients
never lost their state and send no reclaims, so unless those old counts
happen to match, the node holds grace for the full Grace_Period after
the restarted node's clients have reclaimed, and refuses its own
clients' new opens with NFS4ERR_GRACE all that time.

When a clustered node (the backend has maybe_start_grace) enters a grace
period with EVENT_JUST_GRACE, clear the client list and the
RECLAIM_COMPLETE count, and don't hold one extra reaper tick for having
no clients. Lifting still needs try_lift_grace, which for rados_cluster
succeeds only when no node in the grace database needs grace: the
restarted node keeps its NEED flag until its own clients have reclaimed
(or its Grace_Period ends), so nothing is granted to other clients
while those can still reclaim. A restarting node (nfs_start_grace(NULL),
which loads its client list) and takeovers (other events) are unchanged.

---
--- a/src/SAL/nfs4_recovery.c
+++ b/src/SAL/nfs4_recovery.c
@@ -752,6 +752,20 @@
 	if (!gsp && !was_grace) {
 		nfs4_cleanup_clid_entries();
 		nfs4_recovery_load_clids(NULL);
+	} else if (gsp && gsp->event == EVENT_JUST_GRACE && !was_grace &&
+		   recovery_backend->maybe_start_grace) {
+		/*
+		 * EZGH: a clustered node joining a grace period another node
+		 * started. It didn't restart: its clients kept their state and
+		 * won't reclaim, so expect no reclaims (the counts left from
+		 * its own last grace period would hold it for the full
+		 * Grace_Period) and don't hold for the zero-clients case. The
+		 * restarted node's NEED flag in the cluster's grace database
+		 * still keeps every node in grace (try_lift_grace) until that
+		 * node's clients have reclaimed.
+		 */
+		nfs4_cleanup_clid_entries();
+		handling_zero_clients = false;
 	} else if (gsp && gsp->event != EVENT_JUST_GRACE) {
 		/*
 		 * if called from failover code and given a nodeid, then this
